00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:03.340
One of the 3WA's best crime
consultants, Alan Jamis, has died.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:09.020
He spent thirteen years chasing after
an assassin named Sundric.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:17.360
However, in exchange for his life, Alan was
able to leave us one vital piece of information.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.670
It was this:

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:34.450
"Sundric the assassin is certain to be on
Babel flight 107, departing from Planet Solomon."

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:40.410
Come Out, Come Out,
Assassin

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.630
This is air traffic control.
Commence radio check, over.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.390
Roger.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.060
Cabin pressure is normal.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:54.970
All passengers for Babel flight 107 to Pelicide,
please proceed to Gate 7 immediately.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:58.470
All departure procedures
will soon be completed.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.420
Whoops!

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:13.710
Oh?

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:17.250
What a shame, that someone
so beautiful became a nun.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:23.330
If you ever change your mind,
I'll be waiting with open arms, Sister.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.920
Pick up the pace, you old fart!

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.130
O-Old fart?! How dare he!

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.870
Bobbit Huey, the superstar heartthrob...

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:33.400
He's such a hunk!

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:34.930
Sister!

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:41.750
If you really are a servant of God, why don't
you tell him a thing or two about God's teachings?

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.480
Y-You're right.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.140
For cryin' out loud...

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.890
If I recall correctly,
that guy is Marcus, a lawyer.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.330
Marcus Brannigan, 36 years old.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.670
A lawyer, specializing in political trials.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:05.110
He's going to Planet Pelicide to meet with a
certain high-ranking politician for a backroom deal.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.670
Well, now. Acting all goody-goody, aren't we?

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:22.820
Welcome to Babel flight 107, departing from
Planet Solomon. The spacecraft has just lifted off.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:27.780
Please keep your seatbelts fastened
until the seatbelt sign is turned off.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:43.910
That woman is Margaret Tyner, a nurse.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:49.370
And the boy next to her is
her son, Jack Tyner.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.880
Let's see...

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.220
What? The boy's father is unknown?

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:55.550
Hmm...

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:56.520
Pardon me.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:59.930
Mind if I sit down?

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:01.690
G-Go right ahead.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:05.690
Ah, it's always wonderful to have
a lady as your flight companion.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.730
I'm sure...

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:13.780
Ralph Ray. An illustrator, huh?

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.710
What a dull-looking guy.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:30.530
Guess that Ralph guy is
taking his time in the restroom.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.050
Now's my chance!

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:47.770
Sister, you dropped your Bible.

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:54.240
Please be more careful with your belongings.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.650
Don't forget,
we're on a mission!

00:05:56.920 --> 00:06:03.460
Yeah, I know! It's a simple job. I figure out which
one of these passengers is Sundric and nab him.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.430
Bleh!

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:13.670
Captain!

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:14.600
What are you doing?

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:21.610
We're all a disgrace... We're all horrible!

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.080
Die... Turn to ashes!

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:24.180
What's going on? Is something wrong?
Die... Turn to ashes!

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.410
What's going on? Is something wrong?

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.480
Captain, please open the door! Captain!

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:29.450
Please, open the door, Captain!

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.150
Open the door, Captain!

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.680
Everyone, stay back!

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.160
Farewell, angel.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.640
Yuri, look at this.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.520
Everything's been cut, including
the communication circuits.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:05.650
And our course...

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:06.050
Huh?
And our course...

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:06.520
Huh?

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:07.680
Take a look.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:12.360
The flight path has been locked!

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:13.690
It wants a keyword?

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:17.190
At our current speed, in 90 minutes
we're going to run into...

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.970
A black hole...

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:23.200
What's going on?

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:29.140
Did I just hear that we're heading toward
a black hole, and the flight path is locked?

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:31.770
Well?

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:35.820
Don't worry, we'll have the
flight program canceled in no time.

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:38.090
How could this happen?

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.990
I demand an explanation!
We have a right to know!

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:41.420
You're not helping, so just back off!
I demand an explanation!
We have a right to know!

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:42.790
You're not helping, so just back off!

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:49.060
Uh, th-the Lord will protect us.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:50.530
You're the Dirty Pair!

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:54.500
You two are the Dirty Pair from the 3WA, right?

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.500
I saw you in a magazine!

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.970
Oh, is that right?

00:07:57.970 --> 00:07:59.070
Be quiet!

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:02.240
So what if we are?

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:07.240
The energy circuits on the escape shuttle have
been cut, along with the communication circuits.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:09.480
Sundric.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:15.590
I don't know which one of you is Sundric,
but we're in dire need of your help now.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:16.610
Yuri, what are you?

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:20.020
It's true that we came here to arrest you.

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:24.130
But I doubt you want to be swallowed up
by a black hole any more than we do.

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:27.540
Sundric? Sundric is here among us?

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:30.440
Look here. This switch panel
can cancel the flight program.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:34.710
These nine buttons need to be
pressed in a specific pattern,

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:38.680
and the only one here who can
decode it in time is you, Sundric.

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:41.520
What are you talking about? Who's Sundric?

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.350
How do you not know Sundric?

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:46.580
He's an assassin who's known as the
"Cold-Hearted Killing Machine!"

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:49.920
He's also a genius cryptanalyst.

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:59.830
He should reveal himself and crack the code!

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:01.300
Don't you think so, everyone?

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:05.410
Our lives are at stake!
We're just innocent bystanders!

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:09.580
It's none of our concern
whether he gets arrested or not!

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:13.210
Sundric and these two broads should
take their fight elsewhere and leave us out of it!

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:14.510
What did you say?

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:17.120
I'm right, aren't I? What do you think?

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:19.850
If it were me, I wouldn't reveal myself.

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:24.230
I'd kill every single one of you, one by one.

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:25.460
And once everyone was gone...

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:26.130
Stop it!
And once everyone was gone...

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:26.650
Stop it!

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:33.990
Fine. Here's an idea.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.010
Everyone will go to a
different block on this ship.

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:39.140
For twenty minutes,
no one leaves their block.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:43.470
That'll give Sundric time
to decode the program.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.410
Are you sure he's here, though?

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:00.560
You're pretty good. Who taught you?

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.670
Come on, tell me. Your mom? Your teacher?

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:05.100
Hey...

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:08.500
Little brat!

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.710
It-It's an emergency! Ralph is!

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.070
Ralph is escaping in the shuttle!

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:14.010
Come with me!

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:30.590
Don't use the shuttle!
Turn off the power immediately!

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:32.720
It'll explode! Remember what I said?

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:36.130
Enough lies. You can't fool me.

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:39.030
Listen to it. The engine is working just fine!

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:42.560
You idiot! Don't you understand?
The power circuits have been cut!

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:51.940
Farewell Babel 107, you wicked ship!

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:49.700
It shouldn't take Sundric
more than two minutes to decode it.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:52.610
But I wonder if he'll go along with this idea?

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:55.240
I'm sure he's guessed
that we set up spy-eyes.

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:58.580
If I were him, I'd get rid of Kei and me first,
since we're his biggest threats!

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:03.180
Sundric!

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:17.360
Thirteen minutes left...

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:28.730
Wait!

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.450
Marcus? So you're!

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:34.550
No, I'm not! I'm not Sundric!

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:39.820
I thought that maybe if I killed you two,
Sundric would reveal himself.

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:58.400
Ow!

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:02.270
What do you think you're doing,
especially at a time like this?!

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:05.350
Oh, come on, don't be like that, Sister.

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:09.250
Or should I say, Miss Dirty Pair?

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:13.150
We're finally alone, miss.

00:13:14.590 --> 00:13:16.760
What's with you? We're in
the middle of a crisis here!

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:19.190
The danger is what makes it exciting.

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:20.750
It adds to the thrill.

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:24.520
No!

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:30.630
What a let down.
You're nothing but a pervert.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:35.110
I'm not just a pervert.
I'm the world's biggest pervert!

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:37.080
Idiot. I'm too busy with
Sundric to deal with your...

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:37.480
I'm Sundric.
Idiot. I'm too busy with
Sundric to deal with your...

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:39.970
I'm Sundric.

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:42.280
Y-You've gotta be kidding...

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:45.580
However, I've totally fallen for you.

00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:50.010
Depending on your answer, I'll crack the code.

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:52.860
What do you say, miss?

00:13:57.070 --> 00:13:58.670
You don't believe me, do you?

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:01.860
I'll believe the part about you
falling for me, but not the rest.

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.000
You're going to regret it.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:19.380
Mama?

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:21.660
What are you doing?

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:22.950
Jack.

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:32.570
I-It's not what you think.

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:33.940
What do you mean by that?

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:35.930
I... I...

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:39.800
What were you looking for back there?

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:50.750
That man... The Captain...

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:52.520
...was Jack's father.

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:58.590
But, he couldn't have known he had a son.

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:02.400
After all, we separated a long time ago.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:02.660
Was it because of your drug addition?
After all, we separated a long time ago.

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:04.600
Was it because of your drug addition?

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:07.860
There are marks on your neck.

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:12.210
We last saw each other six years ago.

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:14.140
This was all a coincidence.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:18.240
To think, he kept it all this time...

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:31.120
Then, the Captain did all that because...

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:36.220
Most likely, it was
because he saw Jack and me.

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:39.230
Maybe he didn't want to go alone?

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:43.170
Who knows? And there's
no way to ask him now.

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:23.300
3, 6, 2, 8, 4...

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:26.540
4, 6, 2, 5, 3...

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:28.710
It didn't work.

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:30.550
Wait, what was that?

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:32.350
Chief Gooley's number.

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:34.820
This isn't time for jokes, you know.

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:36.560
Sorry, but...

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:39.290
...the question makes absolutely no sense.

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:42.500
"Who does the cute sheep belong to?"

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:52.300
If we're going to escape the
black hole, we have to do it in...

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:55.940
...just seven minutes.

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:03.980
I know pushing buttons randomly
won't solve anything, but...

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:19.590
"Mary Had a Little Lamb?"

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:29.170
Mi-Re-Do-Re-Mi-Mi-Mi...

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:31.150
Re-Re-Re...

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:32.870
Mi-So-So...

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:35.180
Mi-Re-Do-Re...

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:38.750
This is "Mi" and this one's "Re!"

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:41.620
Jack. Who told you to play that song?

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:43.620
Sundric taught you, didn't he?

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:45.990
Never mind that! Hurry up and unlock it!

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:56.400
Huh?

00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:02.010
Shoot.

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:02.240
Don't tell me...
Shoot.

00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:02.840
Don't tell me...

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:03.210
Don't tell me...
The self-destruct switch...

00:18:03.210 --> 00:18:04.710
The self-destruct switch...

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:05.910
...has been activated!

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:10.410
It was set up so that even if we figured out
the code, the ship would self-destruct!

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:11.750
How much time left?

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:12.590
Five minutes.

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:13.990
It's the fourth engine, right?

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:15.890
Hurry, Kei!

00:18:19.230 --> 00:18:20.820
So it was him, after all!

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:29.570
Kei, hurry!

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:31.010
Only three minutes left!

00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:32.170
I know!

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:42.180
Marcus!

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:50.890
It would take you at least
four minutes to defuse this thing.

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:55.760
You're Sundric?!

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:57.990
So the shuttle was empty?

00:18:58.100 --> 00:19:00.200
There was someone on it. Marcus.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:01.960
I killed him and threw him on the shuttle.

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:06.300
The whole reason I was on this ship in the first
place was to kill Marcus, and pose as him.

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:10.880
I have a job to do on Pelicide
which requires taking on his identity.

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:14.980
So you were posing
as Marcus this whole time?

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:19.680
A perfect performance, wasn't it?
Even your partner fell for my act.

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:24.920
Sorry, but...

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:26.630
...I need you dead, too.

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:38.200
Kei, get back inside! We need to fire
the thrusters now, or we won't make it!

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:34.190
Kei!

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:10.360
There are so many things
I still wanted to do, but... Oh, well.

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:12.990
I lived every moment of my life to the fullest.

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:22.970
Miss?

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:25.350
Miss.

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:32.920
You awake now?

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:35.810
Huey...

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:38.350
I told you I've fallen for you, right?

00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:44.330
That pick-up line... How many girls
have you said that to, Bobbit Huey?

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:49.070
You almost died, and that's all you can say?

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:52.870
Feeling special? You can thank
your thoughtful partner for this.

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:55.080
Eavesdropping isn't very thoughtful.

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:55.870
Bleh!

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:59.800
Come now, you should thank
your partner, miss.

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:01.210
Yeah.

00:22:01.780 --> 00:22:04.550
It sure beats dying.

00:22:43.360 --> 00:22:49.860
The mystery began after I fell asleep that time
Ano toki nemuri no ato ni okotta mistuerii

00:22:49.860 --> 00:22:56.400
I was guided by a voice from the future
